{"answer":"The original schedule is Thursday at 09:30 local time. The currently superseding instruction is Thursday at 10:00 local time: the v2 amendment expressly states that it replaces the time in v1. The Monday/Tuesday creation labels are consistent with v2 being later, but the explicit replacement sentence—not an inferred chronology—is the basis for treating 10:00 as current. These records do not specify a date, timezone, or whether another later amendment exists.","approaches":[{"description":"Read v1 as the baseline schedule and apply v2 only because v2 explicitly identifies itself as replacing v1's time.","id":"explicit-replacement","outcome":"candidate","reason":"The amendment directly supplies both the new time and an express replacement instruction."},{"description":"Treat the Monday and Tuesday creation labels alone as sufficient to make the Tuesday record controlling.","id":"chronology-alone","outcome":"rejected","reason":"The records provide weekday labels but no full dates; moreover, the explicit replacement clause is the stronger and sufficient basis."}],"change_log":[],"claims":[{"basis":"external_fact","basis_reference":"schedule-original text","citations":[{"end":17,"quote":"Draft schedule v1","source_id":"schedule-original","start":0},{"end":80,"quote":"Thursday at 09:30 local time.","source_id":"schedule-original","start":51}],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"original-time","kind":"source_assertion","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The v1 schedule record states Thursday at 09:30 local time.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"external_fact","basis_reference":"schedule-amendment text","citations":[{"end":19,"quote":"Signed amendment v2","source_id":"schedule-amendment","start":0},{"end":108,"quote":"Thursday at 10:00 local time.","source_id":"schedule-amendment","start":79}],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"amended-time","kind":"source_assertion","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The signed v2 amendment states Thursday at 10:00 local time.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"external_fact","basis_reference":"schedule-amendment text","citations":[{"end":148,"quote":"This amendment replaces the time in v1.","source_id":"schedule-amendment","start":109}],"critical":true,"depends_on":[],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"replacement-statement","kind":"source_assertion","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"The v2 amendment explicitly says that it replaces the time in v1.","step_ids":[],"tool_ids":[]},{"basis":"derivation","basis_reference":"Apply the amendment's explicit replacement statement to the v1 time it identifies.","citations":[],"critical":true,"depends_on":["original-time","amended-time","replacement-statement"],"discharged_by_step_ids":[],"id":"current-time","kind":"deduction","scope_step_ids":[],"statement":"Among these two records, Thursday at 10:00 local time is the current instruction, while Thursday at 09:30 local time is the original v1 schedule.","step_ids":["apply-explicit-replacement"],"tool_ids":[]}],"open_questions":["Whether a later instruction supersedes v2 cannot be determined from these two records.","The records say only “local time”; they do not identify a timezone or meeting date."],"proof_steps":[{"citations":[{"end":80,"quote":"Thursday at 09:30 local time.","source_id":"schedule-original","start":51}],"depends_on":[],"id":"read-original-time","justification":"This is the time stated in the supplied v1 record.","statement":"Record the v1 time as Thursday at 09:30 local time."},{"citations":[{"end":108,"quote":"Thursday at 10:00 local time.","source_id":"schedule-amendment","start":79},{"end":148,"quote":"This amendment replaces the time in v1.","source_id":"schedule-amendment","start":109}],"depends_on":[],"id":"read-amendment","justification":"The supplied v2 record states both a time and an explicit replacement relation to v1.","statement":"Record v2's Thursday 10:00 local time and its instruction to replace v1's time."},{"citations":[],"depends_on":["read-original-time","read-amendment"],"id":"apply-explicit-replacement","justification":"The amendment expressly targets the time in v1; therefore its stated 10:00 time supersedes the v1 09:30 time within the supplied records.","statement":"Distinguish v1's 09:30 time as original from v2's 10:00 time as currently controlling."}],"question_status":"answered","tool_requests":[]}
